cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this paper or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Heavens Remember: Restoring the Celestial Sermon through Constellation Topography and the Great-Circle Method"
abstract: "The Heavens Remember method paper, version 1.4, in Russian and English, together with the star data its results are computed from. A great-circle scan of the celestial sphere reduces 230,680,184 tested stellar triples to 18,427 unique constellation chains, of which 556 fall at or below 0.001 degrees of cross-track deviation."
